# Store LF in the repository and check LF out, on every platform.
#
# Git's default on Windows is to convert to CRLF on checkout, which makes every
# file read as modified the moment a tool rewrites it with LF, and makes a diff
# between this repo and anything that ran through a Unix tool show the whole file
# changed. The code here is Python and PowerShell; both read LF correctly, so
# there is nothing to gain from the conversion and a lot of noise to avoid.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish: never touch the line endings of an image or a database, even if
# one is ever committed by accident.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.db binary
